# Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for the F1 Analytics Next.js project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package (v2.0.0)
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with the new dependency tree

### 2. Code Integration
**Modified: `app/layout.tsx`**
- Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from '@vercel/speed-insights/next';`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component to the root layout, placed after the existing `<Analytics />` component
- Followed the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router (v13.5+)

## Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel Speed Insights quickstart guide (https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I implemented the recommended setup for Next.js App Router:

1. **Framework Detection**: Identified this as a Next.js 14 project using the App Router
2. **Correct Package Import**: Used `@vercel/speed-insights/next` for optimal Next.js integration
3. **Component Placement**: Added the component at the end of the body tag in the root layout, consistent with the existing Analytics component placement
4. **TypeScript Support**: The package includes full TypeScript support, which integrates seamlessly with the existing TypeScript configuration

## Verification

All verification steps completed successfully:
- ✅ Build completed without errors
- ✅ Linter passed with no warnings or errors  
- ✅ All 308 tests passed (39 test files)
- ✅ No breaking changes introduced

## How It Works

Once deployed to Vercel, Speed Insights will automatically:
- Collect Core Web Vitals and performance metrics
- Track real user monitoring (RUM) data
- Report data to the Vercel dashboard
- Require no additional configuration

The metrics will be visible in the Vercel dashboard under the Speed Insights section after users visit the deployed site.

## Notes

- The implementation preserves all existing functionality
- The SpeedInsights component is lightweight and has minimal impact on bundle size
- Data collection only works when deployed to Vercel
- The component works alongside the existing Vercel Analytics implementation
